    "assessment": {
      "scienceCandidate": "4a917005ff5d39043439c7b530addca3901845fd",
      "scope": "Fresh independent complete23-paragraph B16 reading plus relevant annotations and actual B15/B17, B08 phosphorus and B14 indicator contexts. A bounded reread covered the first nine and second seven paragraphs after9483794 corrections. The final4a917 naming/grammar clarification was checked by the primary agent; no new full independent reread is claimed.",
      "findings": "Separated the full terrestrial pathway involving vascular plants from the separately recommended midpoint. Defined AE, ILCD and Environmental Footprint at their relevant first uses and made deposition load the quantity compared to a critical load. The four headings and unchanged phosphorus boundary continue to work. Soil-component tension and workbook uncertainty remain explicit.",
      "answers": [
        "With critical loads and other conditions fixed, deposition may fall while the affected area stays above threshold. Area-only reporting may remain unchanged while AE records a smaller amount of exceedance. This is no observation of recovery.",
        "One SO2 flow, mass and air class has different CZ/AL stored factors. This refutes a chemistry-only rule for that release, not a specific soil-cause attribution, real damage ratio or cross-method numerical correspondence.",
        "Shared AE naming and the Moles property do not identify the same environmental equivalent. The two NH3 factor ratios differ, so one multiplier cannot reproduce both pairs. Valid model-specific chemical proxy conversions and explicit category weighting are separate questions.",
        "Retain both GLAM descriptions without inferring workbook behavior. The old phosphorus example still converts stipulated applied mass to net freshwater emission once, then uses the matching factor; it cannot supply a coefficient or justify applying loss twice."
      ],
      "limits": "These actual agent answers establish the inspected manuscript interpretation, not empirical learning, original-source completeness, model validity or full PartIV/book completion."
    },
